1.What is text-to-image generation?The process of generating an image from a natural language text description using an AI model.



2.What is image-to-text conversion?The process of generating a textual description or caption from an input image.



3.What is multimodal AI?Artificial intelligence that processes or generates information across multiple modalities such as text, images, audio, and video.



4.Which model is used for text-to-image generation?Stable Diffusion v1.5, a pretrained latent diffusion model.



5.Which model is used for image captioning?BLIP, which stands for Bootstrapping Language-Image Pre-training.



6.What is Stable Diffusion?A latent diffusion model that generates images by progressively denoising latent representations conditioned on text.



7.What is a diffusion model?A generative model that learns to reverse a noise-adding process to generate data.



8.What is a text prompt?A natural language instruction or description provided to guide image generation.



9.What is the purpose of a text encoder?To convert text into numerical representations that the generative model can use.



10.What is image captioning?A vision-language task that generates natural language descriptions of images.



11.What is the role of PyTorch?It provides tensor operations, neural network execution, and GPU acceleration for the pretrained models.



12.What is the purpose of the Diffusers library?It provides implementations and pipelines for diffusion-based generative models.



13.What does guidance scale control?It controls the strength of classifier-free guidance, affecting how closely image generation follows the text condition.



14.What is the difference between text-to-image and image-to-text?Text-to-image generates visual content from text, while image-to-text generates language describing visual content.



15.What are the applications of these models?AI art generation, accessibility, image description, content creation, visual storytelling, and multimodal assistants.
